  "ablation_size_label": "6-case geomean (sizes 1.31M..10.49M bytes; contention 10%, 40%, 90%)",
  "takeaways": [
    "**Single-Launch Last-Man Global Bin Reduction + 128-Bit `uint4` Run-of-4 Collapse (`histogram_lastman_u4_cs256.crisp`):** Replacing the two-launch `output.zero_()` + scalar `uchar` shared-memory baseline (`22.5 µs` on H100) with a single-launch Last-Man pattern (`partials[0..255]` + `ticket` reset to 0 by the last CTA via `atomic-xchg!`), 128-bit `uint4` (16 bytes/load) vectorization, and a per-word Run-of-4 check (`(= w (* (logand w 255u) 16843009u))` -> single `atomic-add! +4u`) cut H100 10 MB runtime by **5.8 µs (−25.8%)** down to **16.7 ± 0.03 µs** (**14.90 µs public geomean**).",
    "**Shared-Memory Replication Tradeoff (4x / 8x vs. 16x Sub-Tables) & Small-Case SM Saturation:** Giving each warp (`wid = tid / 32`, `0..7`) its own 256-bin shared-memory sub-table (8 KB total) eliminates cross-warp shared-memory atomic collisions while keeping per-CTA zeroing and reduction overhead to just 8 `st.shared.b32` / `ld.shared.b32` instructions per thread (`16.7 µs` on H100; **Rank #6 / 20 on L4 at 63.44 µs = 96.8% of #1 genuine**). Doubling to 16 sub-tables (16 KB) increased shared-memory init/reduce overhead to `18.5 µs` on H100, while halving to 4 sub-tables (4 KB) paired with 64B/thread CTA sizing improved B200 from `19.97 µs` down to **17.09 µs** and A100 from `28.90 µs` down to **23.55 µs**.",
    "**Hardware Bit-Field Extraction (`bfe.u32`) via Power-of-2 Division:** Writing byte extraction in Crisp as `(logand (/ w 256u) 255u)` and `(logand (/ w 65536u) 255u)` lowers directly through LLVM NVPTX to single-instruction hardware bit-field extracts (`bfe.u32 %r, %w, 8, 8` and `bfe.u32 %r, %w, 16, 8`), whereas `(ash w -8)` invokes the variable-shift helper `__crisp_ash_uint`.",
    "**Compiler Codegen Bug Identified (`def-function` Returning `=> nil` With Trailing `atomic-add!` inside `if`):** In `histogram_lastman_run16.crisp`, a `def-function` declared `=> nil` whose body contains an `if` expression where one branch ends in `(atomic-add! ...)` and the other ends in a `progn` calling a `=> nil` helper caused an LLVM IR type mismatch in `llc` (`phi` / branch mismatch between `i32` from `atomic-add!` and `void` from `progn`), resolved cleanly by declaring the helper `=> uint` so both branches yield `uint`."
  ],
